1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Wa jê... Ebu Mervan ra silavê...
 
And this... Greetings to Abu Mervan...

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Bavê te Obel dikişîne?
 
Does your father smoke Obel?

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Hacî... Mihemedê Meyî... menî... Xwedê rehma xwe lê ke... ax
jî...
 
Haji... Mihemed of Meyo... I mean... May God have mercy on
him... the earth too...

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Maşallah gundekî bilind e... bilind e... dûr e...
 
Mashallah, it is a high village... it is high... it is
far...

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Li ber vê bayê hênik, maşallah, cew pê pur kîbar e.
 
In this cool wind, mashallah, the weather is very fine.

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Ez hemû xatire miletê me yê Kurdan... şîkî dikim...
 
I [do this] for the sake of all our Kurdish people... I am
filming...

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Înşallah... û hemû jî navê me derkevin.
 
God willing... and may all our names be known.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Yek nivî xwe Şitka bî... baş e... ji dil û can... Şitko.
 
One half of him was from Şitka... okay... with heart and
soul... Şitka.

9
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Merheba hevalno, îro dîsa vîdyoyekî xweş û kîbar em bi we ra
ne.
 
Hello friends, today we are with you again with a nice and
fine video.

10
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Tebean, dost û ehbab û cimeeta... înşallah hemû miroviyê
dilyayê baş dikin hevalno.
 
Of course, friends and loved ones and the community... God
willing all the people of the world are doing well, friends.

11
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Em teqsîrê wê nakin... saeta we xweş... û pir teelîqne xweş
kîbar me ra dişînin.
 
We are not neglecting it... good tidings to you... and you
send us very nice and fine comments.

12
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Çavê we maç dikim.
 
I kiss your eyes.

13
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Îro vîdyoya me jî li gundê... Mezet...
 
Today our video is in the village of... Mezet...

14
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Em li kî derê ne, bêje gundî Şitka bin.
 
Where are we? Say "we are in the village of Şitka".

15
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Merheba hevalên me, hûn çawa ne? Baş in, çawa ne, sihet çawa
ye?
 
Hello our friends, how are you? Are you well, how are
things, how is your health?

16
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Em îro li gundê Şitka ne... Gundê Tatara...
 
Today we are in the village of Şitka... The village of the
Tatars...

17
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Û îro jî hewa pir germ e, hewa qumbele ye.
 
And today the weather is very hot, the weather is [like a]
bomb.

18
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Îro heke dinê ne germ be, bi kêfa xwe em ê bigerin û ji we
re vîdeo bisewirînin.
 
If the world wasn't hot today, we would walk around with
pleasure and film a video for you.

19
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Û inşallah vîdyoya me bihecibînin.
 
And God willing you will like our video.

20
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Înşallah ê bihecibînin.
 
God willing they will like it.

21
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Baş e, hevalno dê bi me ra bin, em têkevin gundê Şitka û em
ji we ra vîdeo çêkin.
 
Okay, friends stay with us, let's enter the village of Şitka
and make a video for you.

22
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Gundê Tatara jî li me bibore, em navê wan hildin... Yalla
wey.
 
And may the village of Tatara forgive us, we mention their
name... Let's go.

23
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Maşallah hevalno tebîeta vî gundî çiqasî xweş e...
 
Mashallah friends, how beautiful the nature of this village
is...

24
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Şitka...
 
Şitka...

25
00:03:46,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Dar û berê gundê Şitka li benda...
 
The trees and surroundings of Şitka village are waiting...

26
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Maşallah, îro jî hewa hênik e, bayê hênik e, xweş e.
 
Mashallah, today the weather is cool too, the wind is cool,
it is nice.

27
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Bes wela hesekî ji mokîna me derdikeve, hesê wek fîtê ye,
nizanim çi ye.
 
But honestly a sound is coming from our car, a sound like a
whistle, I don't know what it is.

28
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Di rêka me ra tê wela.
 
It's coming from our way, honestly.

29
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Dengê maşîna me ye, çi ye...
 
It's the sound of our car, or whatever it is...

30
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Em di ber ra hatin, hata hûlê, paşê em ê jor da lêxînin.
 
We came along the side, up to the slope, then we will hit
upwards.

31
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Em ê herine mala... mala xalê Osman bînim...
 
We will go to the house... I believe Uncle Osman's house...

32
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Em ê bi malbatê jî, malbatê ji me ra xwestibûn.
 
We will [meet] the family too, the family had asked for us.

33
00:06:45,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Em ê herine mala wan, mêvan in îro.
 
We will go to their house, we are guests today.

34
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Wêê, maşallah...
 
Wow, mashallah...

35
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Çi cihe...
 
What a place...

36
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Hevalno we hes kir? Hissê fîtê tê, ji mokîna ye, ji teker e
nizanim ji çi ye.
 
Friends did you hear? A whistling sound is coming, it's from
the car, from the tire, I don't know what it is from.

37
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:29,000
Teq-teqa teker e.
 
It is the clicking of the tire.

38
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Ev cimat da ye.
 
This is the congregation.

39
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Way caga wala... ha babo, ew gotî qabê tişt nîne.
 
Oh empty places... oh father, he said there is nothing in
the container.

40
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:39,000
Were hewş...
 
Come to the yard...

41
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:45,000
Heyrê hewş go... navê, hewş çêkin...
 
Look at the yard he said... no, build a yard...

42
00:12:45,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Barê hewş go, nokî...
 
The load of the yard he said, chickpeas...

43
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Gelpê xerab, gelpê xerab.
 
Bad dog, bad dog.

44
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Hews çêkî, gav ne...
 
You made a yard, the cows didn't...

45
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Mal bi mal...
 
House by house...

46
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Zivistan e, milet rehet rûniştine.
 
It is winter, the people are sitting comfortably.

47
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Rê çêtir e.
 
The road is better.

48
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Rê çêtir e, lê nizanim...
 
The road is better, but I don't know...

49
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Molotof...
 
Molotov...

50
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:50,000
Rêk nîne çêkin.
 
There is no road for them to build.

51
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Mal bi mal ez geriyam, kesî derî venekir.
 
I walked house to house, no one opened the door.

52
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Milo xwedê re hafiz, lê nizanim, welleh rêk nîne çêkin.
 
People, goodbye to God, but I don't know, by God there is no
road to build.

53
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Yanî rêk çêkirina, anû kum şor'a şor'a dikin.
 
Meaning road building, now that they are just messing
around.

54
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Taba mol bi mol... teswîr kim...
 
Of course house by house... I will film...

55
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:32,000
Emê herin...
 
We will go...

56
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Erê hevalno, taba em hatin vî derî, piştî dikan girtî ne, em
li cem xalê min ne.
 
Yes friends, of course we came to this place, since the
shops are closed, we are with my uncle.

57
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Em hinekî destê wî tije bikin, emê hinekî qise bikin.
 
We will shake his hand, we will talk a little.

58
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Bibînin ka behsa çi dike.
 
Let's see what he talks about.

59
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,000
Merheba Xalo.
 
Hello Uncle.

60
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:05,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

61
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:10,000
Xalo vî gundî, hejmara şêniyê gund çiqas malbat in?
 
Uncle, in this village, regarding the number of the
village's residents, how many families are there?

62
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:15,000
Eee hejmara niştecihên gund, teqrîben sed mal e.
 
Eee the number of residents of the village is approximately
one hundred houses.

63
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:19,000
Sed mal. Rind e.
 
One hundred houses. That's good.

64
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Wekî tu jî dizanî, vî çiya nas dikin.
 
As you also know, they know this mountain.

65
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Vî gundî...
 
This village...

66
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Destpêkê vî gundî wexta ku neçêbûye, esasî ye...
 
In the beginning, when this village wasn't built,
basically...

67
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Du bira, du pismam hatin vî gundî.
 
Two brothers, two cousins came to this village.

68
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Yek navê wî Şîto bû. Paşê...
 
One's name was Shito. Then...

69
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Vî digotin Şîtko. Yanî Şîtko.
 
They called him Shitko. Meaning Shitko.

70
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Gund bi navê wî hat naskirin...
 
The village became known by his name...

71
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Ya yek...
 
The one...

72
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:53,000
Qişle bû. Nav lê kirin Qişle.
 
Was a barracks. They named it Qishle.

73
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:58,000
Heta noka vî sırtê me hanê ra dibêjin Qişle.
 
Until now, they call this ridge of ours over there Qishle.

74
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:02,000
Paşê bi çi rengî hat naskirin...
 
Then in what way did it become known...

75
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Bi zeytûnê xwe, bi fêkiyê xwe...
 
By its olives, by its fruits...

76
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,000
...bi rezê xwe, bi tirşê xwe...
 
...by its vineyards, by its sour fruit...

77
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:12,000
...bi henarê xwe, va gunda hat naskirin yanê.
 
...by its pomegranates, this village became known basically.

78
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Kaniya jî heye...
 
There is a spring too...

79
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:19,000
Kaniya jî hebûn vira ser bi lê têl, cem tirba...
 
There were springs here above the wire, near the graves...

80
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:24,000
Wê derê kaniya hebû, xerafe dikirin, berê qontir dikirin...
 
There was a spring there, they maintained it, before they
contracted it...

81
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,000
...xerafe dikirin.
 
...they maintained it.

82
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:29,000
Hene wekî yayla bû.
 
Here was like a summer pasture.

83
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Yanî va gunda, va gunda heta axlerê Cimê jî dihatin...
 
Meaning this village, even the Aghas of Cime came to this
village...

84
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,000
...dihatin vê derê yanê manê.
 
...they came to this place to stay.

85
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,000
Xweş e.
 
That's nice.

86
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Ewê gundiyên rind bûn.
 
Those villagers were good.

87
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Behsa xelkê vira didîn.
 
They praised the people here.

88
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Kalê me jî, e destpêkê Mehmedê Hamo muxtarê gund bû.
 
Our grandfather too, in the beginning Mehmedê Hamo was the
mukhtar of the village.

89
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Yanî xercê camêr bû.
 
Meaning he was a generous man.

90
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Xanêdan bû, xelk dihat malê.
 
He was of noble house, people came to his house.

91
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,000
Yanî bi wê jî... pir hat naskirin.
 
Meaning through him too... it became well known.

92
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Sîleh mîleh jî çêdikirin.
 
They also repaired weapons and things.

93
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Sîlehê kevn...
 
Old weapons...

94
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:05,000
Miletê me vane, huno... li Ewropayê vanê me sêr dikin.
 
Our people are there, you know... in Europe they are
watching us.

95
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:09,000
Yê wulla, ot nê wuno, yanê em ban dikin...
 
Yes, by God, is it not so? Meaning, we call out...

96
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:15,000
...her kes vegere warê gundê xwe, bila gund weke berê dîsa
şên bibin.
 
...for everyone to return to their village home, so the
villages become populated again like before.

97
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Yanê îşda bila kêmkasî di gunda da nemînin.
 
Meaning, so that no deficiencies remain in the villages.

98
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Îşda zehmetê gunda, gundî dimeş... dest me herin. Dijminê
were têkeve.
 
So that the hardship of the villages, the villager walks...
leave our hands. The enemy will come and enter.

99
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:32,000
Em ban êd Ewropayê dikin, li her derkî em banê dikin, miletê
me Kurd bila guh bidin ser cî û warê xwe.
 
We call out to those in Europe, we call out everywhere, let
our Kurdish nation pay attention to their place and home.

100
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,000
Saeta te xweş xalê...
 
Bless you, uncle...

101
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Tu tiştekî dibêjî?
 
Are you saying something?

102
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,000
Gotina te heye, tu tiştekî bikî?
 
Do you have a word, will you add anything?

103
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:43,000
Ez bêjim no wullah, ez çi bikim. Yanê dengê me jî li van
deran bigihîje Kurdê me.
 
I say no, by God, what should I do. Meaning, may our voice
from these places reach our Kurds.

104
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:45,000
Haydê bêje. Tiştek bila werin.
 
Come on, say it. Let them come [back] for something.

105
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:49,000
Yanê wekî gotî, heta kanin, heta wekî gotî jê hewa...
 
Meaning as said, as much as they can, as much as said from
the air...

106
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:55,000
...yanê me'nê qçkê xwe... qçkê xwe hindav nekin, mentiqa xwe
jibîr nekin, gundê xwe jibîr nekin.
 
...meaning, our... let them not lose their kids... let them
not lose their kids, let them not forget their region, let
them not forget their village.

107
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,000
Yanê ev tişt e yê wekî gotî...
 
Meaning this is the thing, as said...

108
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Em vê ro teswîr dikin, em dibên bîrekarî, bila ew na
binînin.
 
We are filming this today, we say it's a souvenir, let them
see this.

109
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Bê guman, yanê roknê... meselen li Ewropayê, yekî dilê xwe
jibîr bikin, yekî herbûbî bibin.
 
Undoubtedly, meaning the corners... for example in Europe,
one forgets their heart, one becomes westernized.

110
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:13,000
Em dixwazin biftilin ser axa xwe, qene bi zimanê... zanin
Kurd in, zanin ser axa xwe ne.
 
We want them to return to their land, at least with the
language... knowing they are Kurds, knowing they are on
their land.

111
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:20,000
Gundê xwe nas bikin, zarokê xwe kokê nas bikin, mîrka nas
bikin, va derdorê va gund nas bikin yanê.
 
To know their village, for their children to know their
roots, to know the nobles, to know these surroundings and
this village, meaning.

112
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,000
Saeta te xweş, Xwedê te ji me ra bihêle.
 
Bless you, may God keep you for us.

113
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:24,000
Saeta we xweş, Xwedê ji we razî be.
 
Bless you, may God be pleased with you.

114
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:28,000
Me marûbe noka, man malê xûlû jî, ji me xwestî, saeta we
xweş, bimînin di xêrê de.
 
Excuse us now, the Khulu family also asked for us, bless
you, stay in goodness.

115
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Me jî kerem kî, em xalîf.
 
You honored us too, we are Khalif.

116
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:35,000
Êv êv, ew darê rûniştine, me qehwa xwe vexwar.
 
Yes yes, they are sitting under the tree, we drank our
coffee.

117
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:45,000
Xaltîk tu dibê çi? Tu silavê dişînî? Tu silavke dikî bişînî?
 
Auntie, what do you say? Are you sending greetings? Will you
send a greeting?

118
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:54,000
E silavê, qîzkê me ra, ji ê de... ji Ebu Hemû wan ra, ji Ebu
Mêrvan ra.
 
Yes greetings, to our daughter, to the... to Abu Hamo and
them, to Abu Mervan.

119
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:58,000
Silavên mi ji giya ra hene. Ez çavê giya maç dikim. Saeta
giya xweş.
 
I have greetings for everyone. I kiss everyone's eyes. Bless
everyone.

120
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:02,000
Xwedê saeta xweş giya de. Gi gul e gul e vegerin malê xwe.
 
May God give everyone a good time. May everyone return to
their home like flowers.

121
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:05,000
Saeta we hezar carî xweş be. Saet xweş mamo.
 
May you be blessed a thousand times. Bless you, uncle.

122
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:25,000
Saet xweş, Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
Bless you, may God be pleased with you.

123
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:38,000
Tu tiştek dibêjî ji neviyên xwe ra? Neviyê te Fawzî heye li
wir.
 
Do you say anything to your grandchildren? Your grandson
Fawzi is there.

124
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:45,000
E silavê ji Fawzî ra, ji xwesiyê Fawzî ra, qîzkê û derê giya
ra hene. Saet xweş.
 
Yes greetings to Fawzi, to Fawzi's mother-in-law, to the
daughter and everyone there. Bless you.

125
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:47,000
Te jî xweş. Silavê te gihîştinê xaltîk.
 
You too. Your greetings have reached them, auntie.

126
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:48,000
E saeta we xweş.
 
Yes, bless you.

127
00:22:48,000 --> 00:23:08,000
Te jî xweş, Xwedê ji te razî be. Ka em herin, hema em li
hewşê kelakê jî...
 
You too, may God be pleased with you. Let's go, let's just
[film] the side of the courtyard too...

128
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:11,000
Maşallah çi ba ye.
 
Mashallah, what a wind.

129
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:13,000
Havalno ba mekin ji vê derê.
 
Friends, don't mention the wind from here.

130
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:33,000
Waye.
 
Here it is.

131
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:03,000
Silav.
 
Greetings.

132
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:04,000
Silav û rêz, ser sera.
 
Greetings and respect, upon my head.

133
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:05,000
Tu çewan î baş î?
 
How are you, are you well?

134
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Tu bi xêr hatî.
 
You are welcome.

135
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:07,000
Baş î, saxî çewan e?
 
Are you well, how is your health?

136
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:08,000
Elhemdulillah.
 
Praise be to God.

137
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:10,000
Êv ha... mala kê ye?
 
This here... whose house is it?

138
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:12,000
Êv mala Hamo ye. Hamo... Hamo mezin.
 
This is Hamo's house. Hamo... Hamo the Elder.

139
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:13,000
Hamo mezin.
 
Hamo the Elder.

140
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:17,000
Hamo bavê Hesen. Hesen bavê Ehmed.
 
Hamo the father of Hesen. Hesen the father of Ahmed.

141
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:18,000
Ê maşallah.
 
Oh Mashallah.

142
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:20,000
Mala Hamo ye.
 
It is Hamo's house.

143
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:22,000
Êv dîwarê kevn e, dîwarê berê ye.
 
This is an old wall, a wall from the past.

144
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:23,000
Êv dîwarê kevn e.
 
This is an old wall.

145
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:25,000
Zîkriyatê xwe vir da pir ne?
 
Are your memories here many?

146
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:30,000
Êvê hewşê da, zikriyet mezin bûn û...
 
In this courtyard, memories grew and...

147
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:38,000
Ciyê tilyê mezin bûn, li vî derî, xal... xalê Mihemed. Em
man ev hewşa we ye.
 
The place of the big fingers (prominent people) were here,
Uncle... Uncle Muhammed. We assume this is your courtyard.

148
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:40,000
Ev hewşa me ye.
 
This is our courtyard.

149
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:44,000
Kîbar e.
 
It is elegant.

150
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:46,000
Mala Hac Cemîl e.
 
It is Hajj Jamil's house.

151
00:24:46,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Mala Hac Cemîl jî me teswîr kir wera?
 
Did we film Hajj Jamil's house with you too?

152
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:09,000
Maşallah, şînkayî tê da rind e.
 
Mashallah, the greenery inside is nice.

153
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:10,000
Şînkayî tê da heye.
 
There is greenery inside.

154
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:13,000
Hewşek pir xweş e.
 
It is a very nice courtyard.

155
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:14,000
Hinar û tişt.
 
Pomegranates and things.

156
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:15,000
Hinar û tişt.
 
Pomegranates and things.

157
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:16,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

158
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:19,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

159
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:22,000
Êv ciyê, dibê mala Apê Teyar?
 
This place, do they say it's Uncle Teyar's house?

160
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:25,000
Mala Apê Teyar.
 
Uncle Teyar's house.

161
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:26,000
Kerem ke.
 
Please (go ahead).

162
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:28,000
Em herin jor?
 
Shall we go up?

163
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:31,000
Na, em anî zûrin vê... teswîr dikin.
 
No, we will zoom in on this... film it.

164
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

165
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:52,000
Hewşa xwe kîbar e.
 
Its courtyard is elegant.

166
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:33,000
Hewşa xwe pir kîbar e. Hêşinayî tê da rind e, û mentiqa xwe
jî rind e.
 
Its courtyard is very elegant. The greenery inside is nice,
and its location is also nice.

167
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:37,000
Ciyê xwe xweş e. Hewşe... li xerbê gund e.
 
Its place is nice. The courtyard... is in the west of the
village.

168
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:42,000
Li pêşiya ahiq e, pîşiya me em vêra dibên Geliye Cerjim,
heta Cerjim dere êv.
 
It is in front of the horizon, in front of us we call this
the Valley of Cerjim, this goes until Cerjim.

169
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:44,000
Heta Sênorê dere.
 
It goes until the Border.

170
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Sênorê, di pîşiya me ye.
 
The Border, is in front of us.

171
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:49,000
Wulla kîbar çêkiriye, maşallah.
 
By God, he made it elegantly, Mashallah.

172
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:56,000
Vêra dibên... devê yol... em vêra dibên derê Geliye Cerjim.
 
They call this... the road mouth... we call this the
entrance of the Valley of Cerjim.

173
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:58,000
Wê tilyê li hember te, dibê Tilê Attara?
 
That hill opposite you, is it called the Hill of Attars?

174
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:00,000
Tilê Attara.
 
The Hill of Attars.

175
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:11,000
Tilê Attara, hevalno, ew cara di bîstin Tilê Attara. Ka wera
em vir va jî herin. Xal wera.
 
The Hill of Attars, friends, you hear about the Hill of
Attars sometimes. Come, let's go this way too. Uncle come.

176
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:14,000
Êv Qişle ye. Em dibên Qişle.
 
This is the Barracks. We call it the Barracks.

177
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:17,000
Êv sirtê panik e. Em dibêjin sirtê panik.
 
This is the wide ridge. We call it the wide ridge.

178
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:22,000
Maşallah, no no. Kîbar çêkiriye.
 
Mashallah, no no. He made it elegantly.

179
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:25,000
Êv ciyê behs e. Masbah e.
 
This is a place of leisure. It's a resort.

180
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:45,000
Êv ciyê behs e.
 
This is a place of leisure.

181
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:31,000
Merhaba xaltîk.
 
Hello auntie.

182
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:33,000
Merhaba.
 
Hello.

183
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Tu çewan î, baş î?
 
How are you, are you well?

184
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:38,000
[Unintelligible].
 
[Unintelligible].

185
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:44,000
Tu baş î?
 
Are you well?

186
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:45,000
Te go çi?
 
What did you say?

187
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:46,000
[Unintelligible].
 
[Unintelligible].

188
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:51,000
Wera wera, merd xaltîka te hêl kin u ştî çin û ştî.
 
Come come, let the men leave your aunt alone and things go
and things.

189
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:53,000
Ez dibêm merd xaltîka te hêl kin ştî hêl kin.
 
I say let the men leave your aunt alone, let the thing
alone.

190
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:55,000
Tiştî, merê ra dî, merê ke...
 
The thing, saw the husband, the husband that...

191
00:28:55,000 --> 00:29:02,000
Erê, merd xaltîka te hêl kem cîckê şirîn.
 
Yes, let the men leave your aunt alone, sweet little one.

192
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:04,000
Maşallah, ava xwe ma kêm nabe, ava xwe nake.
 
Mashallah, its water doesn't decrease, its water doesn't
[stop].

193
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:07,000
Ava xwe kêm nabe, tebîe ye.
 
Its water doesn't decrease, it is natural.

194
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:09,000
Kê diket bîra ko...
 
Who remembers that...

195
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:29,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

196
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:49,000
Av xweş e?
 
Is the water good?

197
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:50,000
Av sar e, sar.
 
The water is cold, cold.

198
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:53,000
Ev loqê... loqê avê ye na?
 
This spout... is a water spout, right?

199
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:54,000
Ev loqê avê ye.
 
This is a water spout.

200
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:55,000
Loqê avê ye.
 
It is a water spout.

201
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:56,000
Dîkora nîse, ser...
 
It's a nice decor, on...

202
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:57,000
Dîkora nîse ser çavê me.
 
A nice decor, upon our eyes.

203
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:59,000
Deynê ser tilyan ser hewşê kin.
 
Put the view on the fingers (details) on the courtyard.

204
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Deynê ser tilyan ser hewşê kin.
 
Put the view on the fingers (details) on the courtyard.

205
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Kerem ke falo, te digot çi?
 
Go ahead uncle, what were you saying?

206
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:09,000
Te digot hewşî mokhtêr e...
 
You were saying the Mukhtar's courtyard...

207
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:12,000
Deng.
 
Voice [Speak up].

208
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:18,000
Cem... Cem apê Hesen, Cem apê Tîrêj, Cem Ozanê...
 
Cem... Cem uncle of Hesen, Cem uncle of Tîrêj, Cem Ozan...

209
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:23,000
Bapîrê rênas, bavkê rênas.
 
Renas's grandfather, Renas's father.

210
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Mokhtarê me yê kevn, ava hewşa xwe bû.
 
Our old Mukhtar, this was his courtyard.

211
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:34,000
Mihemed... Mihemed Huseyn.
 
Mohammed... Mohammed Huseyn.

212
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:39,000
Navê bavê... navê Mihemed yê aşê...
 
The father's name... the name of Mohammed of the mill...

213
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:40,000
Navê metê me ye.
 
It's our aunt's name.

214
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:46,000
Bavê Huseyn. Xwedê rehma xwe lê ke, ava cihê xoyî mezin e.
 
Huseyn's father. May God have mercy on him, this was his
grand place.

215
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:52,000
Eses rewşa gundan ke, osad mokhtar û Mihemedê me yê mezin...
 
Basically the situation of the villages, the master Mukhtar
and our great Mohammed...

216
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:59,000
Xwedê rehma xwe lê ke. Hewş jî di vî mentiqê da... di nav vî
tenîştê...
 
May God have mercy on him. The courtyard too, in this
area... within this side...

217
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:00,000
Kerem ke falo.
 
Go ahead, uncle.

218
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:03,000
Spas dikim, ser çava.
 
Thank you, you're welcome.

219
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:05,000
Ava mala mokhtarê me yê kevn e.
 
This is the house of our old Mukhtar.

220
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:08,000
Yanî ji bavkê xwa da, ji kalkê xwa da.
 
Meaning, from his father, from his grandfather.

221
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:16,000
Mokhtar leqet dikirin. Berê meclis, kalkê 'emûl... pêşiya
dîwanê firdanke.
 
They were elected Mukhtar. Before the council, the
worker's... before the court/assemblies.

222
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:19,000
Ava mala xwa esasî a kevn e.
 
This is their original old house.

223
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:24,000
Hîn kalkê xwa têda bû, bavkê xwa têda bû, mokhtar têda bû,
mokhtar jî rehmetî bû.
 
When his grandfather was in it, his father was in it, the
Mukhtar was in it, and the Mukhtar passed away.

224
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:30,000
Ava jî kulfeta xwa ye, li şûna mayî. Xwedê jê dînimîne,
merim neke.
 
This is his family, remaining in his place. May God not
leave them without faith, nor without people.

225
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:31,000
Xwedê jê razî be.
 
May God be pleased with him.

226
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:33,000
Amîn, amîn.
 
Amen, amen.

227
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Û mokhtarê gund bû, umûrê gund gi dimeşandin.
 
And he was the village Mukhtar, he managed all the village
affairs.

228
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:37,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

229
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:40,000
Umûrê gund gi dimeşandin, cara beşer ji gund jî nêşî...
 
He managed all the village affairs, sometimes people from
the village [would be upset]...

230
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:43,000
Yanî milet jê razî bû?
 
So the people were pleased with him?

231
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:44,000
Heyran, beşer cara jî nêşî bûn.
 
My dear, sometimes people were [unhappy/upset].

232
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Mezni xwa jê razî bûn.
 
Their elders were pleased with him.

233
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:50,000
Yanî çiq meznî xwa jê razî bûn, gî jî dihatin şêwra xwa pê
dikirin.
 
Meaning, however much their elders were pleased with him,
everyone came and consulted with him.

234
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:53,000
Mokhtar gî ya dihat şêwra xwa pê dikir.
 
The Mukhtar, everyone would come and consult with him.

235
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:57,000
Û şevra... bi kêra... bigo tavînkê hena bi meşin hena...
 
And [he spent] his nights... with effort... saying until the
sun [rises] let's walk...

236
00:31:57,000 --> 00:32:00,000
Vêra muwafeq bûn, û vêra yanî...
 
They agreed on this, and on this meaning...

237
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:01,000
Tecewûb dikirin.
 
They responded/cooperated.

238
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:04,000
Rind e. Yanî mokhtar gerek wena bin.
 
It is good. Meaning, Mukhtars should be like that.

239
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:08,000
Yanî mokhtarê me, belkî divê mentiqê tevda da, wek mokhtarê
me tune bû.
 
Meaning our Mukhtar, perhaps in this entire region, there
was no one like our Mukhtar.

240
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:15,000
Navê xwa Mihemed bû, me digot... me digot Mokhtar yanî. Navê
xwa esasî Mihemed bû.
 
His name was Mohammed, we called him... we just said
Mukhtar. His original name was Mohammed.

241
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:21,000
Wekî din, livê derê, yanî umûrek biba, mişkîlek biba, der
biba...
 
Otherwise, in this place, meaning if there was a matter, a
problem, a trouble...

242
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:29,000
Tavilê çend rîspiyê gund dikirin, digotin xayû werin em
herin vê de'wiyê, vê mişkîlê em hel kin yanî.
 
Immediately he would gather a few village elders, saying
"Brothers come, let's go to this dispute, let's solve this
problem."

243
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:31,000
Erê. Çi girêk ba vedikir?
 
Yes. Whatever knot [problem] there was, he untied it?

244
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:39,000
Çi girêkî ba, bi destî wî bû, wî jî bang... bang xêrî xwa,
êd mezin xwa dikir, digot werin em herin vê mişkîlê hel kin
yanî.
 
Whatever knot there was, it was in his hands, he would
call... call his good people, his elders, saying "Come let's
go solve this problem."

245
00:32:39,000 --> 00:32:40,000
Xizmet milet dikir.
 
He served the people.

246
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:42,000
Xizmet karê wî miletî bû.
 
His job was serving this people.

247
00:32:42,000 --> 00:32:43,000
Bravo. Xwedê rehma xwe lê ke.
 
Bravo. May God have mercy on him.

248
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:49,000
Xwedê rehma xwa lê ke, cihê xwa cenet be. Îsanekî pirî
ekabir, kîbar bû.
 
May God have mercy on him, may his place be paradise. He was
a very noble, polite person.

249
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:54,000
Welhemdulillah, kurê xwa jî rabûyîne, lawê xwa mezin, lawê
xwa mezin Adnan e.
 
And praise be to God, his son has also grown up, his eldest
son, his eldest son is Adnan.

250
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:57,000
Şûna bavkê girtî. Hew jî pir însanê kîbar e.
 
He took his father's place. He is also a very polite person.

251
00:32:57,000 --> 00:33:01,000
Û d'pêra heva, Dilû hew jî lawê xwa yê biçûk e...
 
And after him, Dilu (Delovan) is also his younger son...

252
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Lawê xwa yê ji wî ciçiktir e, hew jî waye xizmet û mêrê
diwan û gunda va kirî.
 
His son who is younger than him, he is also there serving, a
man of the court/guest house and the villages.

253
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:11,000
Xizmetî vî gundî gî dibîne. Yanî saeta giya xweş, şev û mal
xwa ji ber e da...
 
He sees to the service of this whole village. Meaning health
to everyone, he puts his night and home aside...

254
00:33:11,000 --> 00:33:13,000
Li ser kolkê ji we ra deran dakin.
 
They open doors for you [even] in the hut.

255
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:19,000
Elane, sê sed... şêş şêş. Efrîn şêş şêş.
 
Now, three hundred... six six. Afrin six six [likely
referring to code 66].

256
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:27,000
Em pir ji we qenelê razî ne. Wayê hatine nava miletê me,
teswîr dikin.
 
We are very pleased with your channel. You have come among
our people, filming.

257
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:30,000
Rind û xerab, wîngî dikşînin...
 
Good and bad, you are filming it all...

258
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:34,000
Derdê me û kulê me hûn derdixin derê, yanî...
 
You are bringing our troubles and grief out [to the world],
meaning...

259
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:39,000
Tiştekî rind e, û alem tevdal Ewrûpa û dera gî li me seyir
dikin, gî me dibînin.
 
It is a good thing, and the whole world in Europe and
everywhere is watching us, everyone sees us.

260
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Soyke hatine gundê xwa, me xwa dibînin yanî.
 
It is as if they have come to their village, they see
us/themselves.

261
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:43,000
E bira me kirî jî em e bibînin.
 
And those we missed, we will see them.

262
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:46,000
E bira me kirî jî em e bibînin. Saeta we xweş.
 
And those we missed, we will see them. Health to you.

263
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:52,000
Bimînin di xweşiyê de. Em kan gundê din jî? Gundê kêlekê?
 
Stay in happiness/peace. Shall we go to the other village
too? The village next door?

264
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:56,000
Em kan Tatar a... teben Tatar a jêr e?
 
Let's go to Tatar... naturally Lower Tatar?

265
00:33:56,000 --> 00:34:00,000
Erê Tatar a, teqrîben du pênc kîlometre, du du kîlometre
mişkî anha dûr e.
 
Yes Tatar, approximately two-five kilometers, two-two
kilometers walking from here.

266
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:02,000
Bi xatirê te.
 
Goodbye to you.

267
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:04,000
Oxir be, oxir be.
 
Bon voyage, bon voyage.

268
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:07,000
De oxir be.
 
Okay, bon voyage.

269
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:08,000
Destê we sax be.
 
Health to your hands [Thank you].

270
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:11,000
Saeta we xweş, ev o hevalno mala mamoyê...
 
Health to you, friends this was Uncle's house...

271
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:13,000
We xwarin nexwariye.
 
You haven't eaten food.

272
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:15,000
Na wallah, em çayekê... yekê vexwin ka bes e.
 
No by God, if we drink a tea... one, that is enough.

273
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:20,000
Xwedê pêxember ji we razî be, xwaştek saet xweş. Em rabin
cemek xalê xwe.
 
May God and the Prophet be pleased with you, wish you a good
time. Let's get up [and go] to our uncle.

274
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:23,000
Saeta we xweş, gulê gulan.
 
Health to you, rose of roses [dear one].

275
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:24,000
Silaq kim.
 
Let me greet [shake hands].

276
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:27,000
Xwedê te bişêwîne, Xwedê we biparêze.
 
May God beautify you, may God protect you.

277
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:29,000
Saeta we xweş. Xwedê pêxember ji we razî be.
 
Health to you. May God and the Prophet be pleased with you.

278
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:31,000
Saet xweş.
 
Good health.

279
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:35,000
Erê hevalno, teben ev hatine nişte gundê Tatar a.
 
Yes friends, naturally we have come to the descent of the
village of Tatar.

280
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:40,000
Tatar a jî, ba mekin e gelî, li hew kî vîr da fi re, gelî
gelî.
 
Tatar too, look at the place friends, over there turn
around, look look.

281
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:45,000
Maşallah gundekî bilind e, bilind e, dûr e. Ar... teqrîben
pêncî kîlometre em hatin.
 
Mashallah, it is a high village, high and far. About...
approximately fifty kilometers we came.

282
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:49,000
Maşallah deşta Ceme bîne? Ooo Cindirêsê li rûyî li ko.
 
Mashallah, do you see the plain of Ceme (Jeme)? Ooo,
Jinderis is facing over there.

283
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:51,000
Ba mekin, ez nikanim.
 
Look, I can't [believe it].

284
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:54,000
Hevalno tebîeta vî gundî pir xweş e, kîbar e.
 
Friends, the nature of this village is very nice, very
elegant.

285
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:56,000
Seke, Cindirês li rûyî li ko.
 
Look, Jinderis is facing over there.

286
00:34:56,000 --> 00:34:59,000
Ewwel merre ez têm vî... vî mentiqê.
 
First time I come to this... this region.

287
00:34:59,000 --> 00:35:03,000
Dûr e, hewşî mirov ket pêşiya me welle, ez nizanim gotin ma.
 
It's far, someone's courtyard fell in front of us really, I
don't know if they told us.

288
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:07,000
Çend mal ne, pir ne... ewa mezin e.
 
There are a few houses, not many... that big one.

289
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:10,000
Heta cawê te ferdike seke mentiqê me. Maşallah.
 
As far as your eye can see, look at our region. Mashallah.

290
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:12,000
Tebîetek pir xweş e.
 
A very nice nature.

291
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:14,000
Û bo jî mekin e.
 
And look down there too.

292
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:15,000
Ehê...
 
Aha...

293
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:17,000
Ya selam.
 
Oh peace [Wow].

294
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:19,000
Teben evnana jî gi çadir ne hevalno.
 
Naturally, all these are tents, friends.

295
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:22,000
Evana muxeyemat ne, çêkirine.
 
These are camps, they have built them.

296
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:24,000
Ji miletê me, sawê tilî.
 
From our people, because of the earthquake [or
displacement].

297
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:25,000
Eh...
 
Eh...

298
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:28,000
Hewalî viko lexta kamerê li gund bigir, bisawirîne.
 
Friend, take a shot of the village with the camera, film it.

299
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:30,000
[Man shouting in background]
 
[Man shouting in background]

300
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:47,000
Ooh...
 
Ooh...

301
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:48,000
Silaqet 'ele nebî.
 
Peace be upon the Prophet [Wow].

302
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:50,000
Ji vî gundî ra...
 
For this village...

303
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:52,000
Em di ber hatin a hevalno, gelî?
 
We came through here friends, look?

304
00:35:52,000 --> 00:35:54,000
Gi kaş... gi kaş.
 
All uphill... all uphill.

305
00:35:54,000 --> 00:35:57,000
Dorê merxê jî gi av kirine.
 
Around the chicken coop, they have watered it all.

306
00:35:57,000 --> 00:36:01,000
Wer vê ketî, çi biyî ez nizanim.
 
Come this way, what happened I don't know.

307
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:02,000
[Child screaming playfully]
 
[Child screaming playfully]

308
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:21,000
Helê ne.
 
Go.

309
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:25,000
Erê hevalno, teben vî gundî da jî hewş pir xirab e hene?
 
Yes friends, naturally in this village too, the situation is
very bad, right?

310
00:36:25,000 --> 00:36:29,000
Gî çend mal ne, yanî. Ne pir ne.
 
There are only a few houses, meaning. Not many.

311
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:31,000
Kako ma çend mal... mal batin ne vî gundî?
 
Brother, how many houses... are in this village?

312
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:33,000
Çend hewş ne?
 
How many courtyards?

313
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:36,000
Em sê kurmanc in, yek ereb e.
 
We are three Kurds, one is Arab.

314
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:39,000
Yanî mal... mal çiqas hene, bîst mal hene vî gundî?
 
Meaning houses... how many houses are there, are there
twenty houses in this village?

315
00:36:39,000 --> 00:36:40,000
Mal gi? Ha xwedê nizanim.
 
Houses in total? By God I don't know.

316
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:41,000
Gi xirabine ler?
 
Are they all ruined?

317
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:43,000
Mal piranî vala ne.
 
Most houses are empty.

318
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:46,000
Ê sox tane? Ha bas çar mal in.
 
The inhabited ones? Ah, just four houses.

319
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:47,000
Malê sox?
 
Inhabited houses?

320
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:48,000
Mala... nîzamî tane, çar mal in.
 
The house of... properly, there are four houses.

321
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:49,000
Çar mal sox ne lo?
 
Four inhabited houses, really?

322
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Çar mal tane, livir ne.
 
Four houses only, they are here.

323
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Çar mal, evne du mal, malê ewê kevn e.
 
Four houses, these two houses, that one is an old house.

324
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:56,000
Wekî vê malê, ha va kes tê tüne.
 
Like this house, no one is in it.

325
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:58,000
Malê serbas kes tê tüne.
 
The house above, no one is in it.

326
00:36:58,000 --> 00:36:59,000
Malê bavê Huseyn...
 
Huseyn's father's house...

327
00:36:59,000 --> 00:37:01,000
Çar mal bas divî derê da tane hene, dijîn.
 
Only four houses are actually here, living.

328
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:04,000
Malê Ebû Seid ew jî Ereb hatiye û nazihîn hatiye cema.
 
Abu Seid's house, he is an Arab who came, displaced people
came to the gathering.

329
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:07,000
Û zutim mala bavê Huseyn û malê xalê Ebbo...
 
And I said Huseyn's father's house and Uncle Ebbo's house...

330
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:08,000
Pismamî Ebdilnebiye.
 
It's Ebdilnebi's cousin.

331
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:09,000
Pismamê me ne, pismamê Ebdilnebiye.
 
They are our cousins, Ebdilnebi's cousins.

332
00:37:09,000 --> 00:37:11,000
Bes em tanî kurmanc in?
 
Are only we [you] Kurds?

333
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:12,000
Em kurmanc in, em pismam in.
 
We are Kurds, we are cousins.

334
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:13,000
E em Ereb in, eslê me Ereb e.
 
[Joke/Sarcasm] Eh we are Arabs, our origin is Arab.

335
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:14,000
Tu kurmancî zanî?
 
Do you know Kurmanji?

336
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:15,000
Bas em j'vir re dijîn e.
 
But we live here.

337
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:16,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

338
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:18,000
Tu li dere berva dixwînî?
 
Do you study outside?

339
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:19,000
Na, ez naçim.
 
No, I don't go.

340
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:20,000
Te dere ber nexwindiye?
 
You haven't studied outside?

341
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:21,000
Te dere ber.
 
[Repeating] Outside.

342
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:22,000
Ewa, te dere ber?
 
Yes, you [mean] outside?

343
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:24,000
Ewa da em berda daxwînin.
 
Yes, we study [nearby/here].

344
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:26,000
Ewa.
 
Yes.

345
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:29,000
Şivonki mezin e.
 
A big shepherd [dog].

346
00:37:29,000 --> 00:37:31,000
Keçkê, te digot ka...
 
Girl, you were saying where...

347
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:33,000
Wela lezim e kî bızine begî dimrin.
 
By God, it's necessary, otherwise the goats will all die.

348
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:34,000
Xêr e?
 
What's wrong?

349
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Gi teba ta çûye li qizna yê lê.
 
All the nature/animals went to the girl's side over there.

350
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:37,000
Aaa kepek.
 
Aaa dog.

351
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:38,000
Aywa, gi diçin.
 
Yes, they all go.

352
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:41,000
Are ab cernokno jî kevn e.
 
Yes, these basins are also old.

353
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:43,000
Ehê...
 
Aha...

354
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:45,000
Seke av têdaye ho.
 
Look there is water in it, look.

355
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:47,000
Ava me'nî dewer e avo?
 
This means [it's for] beasts, this one?

356
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:49,000
Awa, ney. Ji bo nan, ji bo nan çêkirin e.
 
Yes, no. For bread, for making bread.

357
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:51,000
Awa me'nî dewer e, dewer têd av dida, sese ne.
 
This means beasts, beasts were given water in it, right.

358
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:54,000
Berê hona bî, gîştek hona bî.
 
Before it was like this, everything was like this.

359
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:56,000
Keçkê av der çiye?
 
Girl, what is this place?

360
00:37:56,000 --> 00:37:57,000
Mala me ye.
 
It is our house.

361
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:58,000
Malawate?
 
Your house?

362
00:37:58,000 --> 00:37:59,000
Mala me ya kevn e.
 
Our old house.

363
00:37:59,000 --> 00:38:00,000
Mala we ya kevn e?
 
Your old house?

364
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:01,000
Ewa.
 
Yes.

365
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:03,000
Wallah maşallah.
 
By God, Mashallah.

366
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:04,000
Avana gî kevn e, seke.
 
These are all old, look.

367
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Biznê me ya rind bîn bare sor?
 
Were our goats good with the red load?

368
00:38:06,000 --> 00:38:07,000
Kujone heve?
 
Which one is it?

369
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:09,000
He... heve. Berê kuro der.
 
Ah... that one. Before [the boy] took it out.

370
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:10,000
E mexê mokino xora wirziknîne le?
 
Hey, didn't you hide your machines/stuff?

371
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:12,000
Niş na be, mala me ya ava ne.
 
It won't work, our house is that one.

372
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:16,000
Vîng e, dika vim bê gelîkî... dixwazim rînî bikolim ada.
 
Look, I want to see a view... I want to sit and dig in it.

373
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:17,000
Oboooo, vexwame tê da!
 
Ohhh, there is [something] inside it!

374
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:19,000
Ehê, tediyê?
 
Aha, you see?

375
00:38:19,000 --> 00:38:20,000
Heva.
 
This one.

376
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:22,000
Ne heva.
 
Not this one.

377
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:24,000
Avolî mli bgir wela, hewşa kevnar livir jî hene?
 
Friend film it, really, are there old courtyards here too?

378
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:27,000
Ava zilzal hatinî.
 
This one, the earthquake came [hit it].

379
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:28,000
Bxê bî zilzal hat?
 
Did the earthquake really come?

380
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:29,000
Zilzal.
 
Earthquake.

381
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:30,000
Zilzal lê da he?
 
The earthquake hit it, huh?

382
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:31,000
Ewa, zilzal lê da.
 
Yes, the earthquake hit it.

383
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:32,000
Xwedê emîne!
 
Aunt Emine! [Likely misidentifying someone or shouting a
name].

384
00:38:32,000 --> 00:38:34,000
Ewa jina pismamê bavê min e.
 
That is the wife of my father's cousin.

385
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:37,000
Are hevale me taşme xwest, teben em gîşta pismam û malbatê
wa...
 
Yes friend, we wanted [something], naturally we are all
cousins and family...

386
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:39,000
Hev malbata tey?
 
Is this your family?

387
00:38:39,000 --> 00:38:42,000
Zikryatê te lver pir ne.
 
Your memories here are many.

388
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:45,000
Av hewşa teben qîzik meriv vê zilzalê hedimondî?
 
This courtyard, naturally girl, did this earthquake destroy
it?

389
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:46,000
E...
 
Yes...

390
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:48,000
Lexî me lexî qêpixe.
 
Hit it, hit the door [knock].

391
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:52,000
Xotke Emîne!
 
Aunt Emine!

392
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:54,000
Xotke Emîne!
 
Aunt Emine!

393
00:38:54,000 --> 00:38:56,000
Xotke nêj nêvr qirî qîzek ne l'mal e.
 
Aunt is not... the girl is not home.

394
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:57,000
Feqîr e?
 
Is she poor?

395
00:38:57,000 --> 00:39:00,000
Xotke Emîne!
 
Aunt Emine!

396
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:02,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

397
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:07,000
Avolî we diyiye, dor dor kî hêl bın, dor, henderî bo mekin
vê gundî.
 
Friend you saw, surrounded by trees, look at the
surroundings of this village.

398
00:39:07,000 --> 00:39:08,000
Oooh.
 
Oooh.

399
00:39:08,000 --> 00:39:10,000
Hev hewşo jî kevnar e ho.
 
This courtyard is also ancient, look.

400
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:12,000
Awolî muko were.
 
Friend come here.

401
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:14,000
Wê bigre.
 
Film it.

402
00:39:14,000 --> 00:39:18,000
Seke gundo êzingê xwa çû disafînin.
 
Look, the village has stacked their firewood.

403
00:39:18,000 --> 00:39:21,000
Çîlçûk.
 
Chick [calling chickens].

404
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:22,000
Were.
 
Come.

405
00:39:22,000 --> 00:39:24,000
Çû çû çû çû.
 
Chu chu chu [calling chickens].

406
00:39:24,000 --> 00:39:25,000
Xor e.
 
It eats.

407
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:28,000
Ha kesek risqê xwa digere te diyiye?
 
Look, everyone seeks their sustenance, you see?

408
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:31,000
Mirîşka çêkirine.
 
The chickens have made [nests].

409
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:33,000
Migo kê pê risqê xwa ketin ho.
 
I said who fell into their sustenance, look.

410
00:39:33,000 --> 00:39:38,000
Heta çêlçûk jî li risqê xwa digerin, pê risqê xwa ketine.
 
Even the chicks are looking for their sustenance, they are
after their sustenance.

411
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:39,000
Dest nede.
 
Don't touch.

412
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:41,000
Ooo.
 
Ooo.

413
00:39:41,000 --> 00:39:42,000
Vaye?
 
Is it there?

414
00:39:42,000 --> 00:39:43,000
Hêlîn.
 
Nest.

415
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:44,000
Çar hêlîn kirine.
 
They made four nests.

416
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:46,000
Hêlîn çêkirine?
 
They made nests?

417
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:47,000
Ewa.
 
Yes.

418
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:51,000
Are avolîno, hêlîn obinrin, hêlîn, mirîşka çar hêlîn kirine.
 
Yes friends, look at the nests, nests, the chickens made
four nests.

419
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:52,000
Gerek evna xiste me bin.
 
These should be [assigned/given] to us.

420
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:54,000
Çar hêlîn kirine mirîşke.
 
The chicken made four nests.

421
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:55,000
Yek, du, sê, çar.
 
One, two, three, four.

422
00:39:55,000 --> 00:39:57,000
Yek, du, sê, çar.
 
One, two, three, four.

423
00:39:57,000 --> 00:39:58,000
Are.
 
Yes.

424
00:39:58,000 --> 00:40:00,000
Em gîştin...
 
We reached...

425
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:05,000
Haho, welatê me nexweş e, em hatine ba te, emê niha koçberê
te bikin.
 
Oh my, our country is unwell, we have come to you, we are
going to make you a refugee now.

426
00:40:05,000 --> 00:40:10,000
Welatê me nexweş e, emê te bikin penaber. Werin wêne çêkin.
 
Our country is unwell, we will make you a refugee. Come,
take a picture.

427
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:13,000
Emê we mecbûr bikin, tişt di dest de heye?
 
We will force you, do you have anything in your hand?

428
00:40:13,000 --> 00:40:15,000
Tişto, tişto na.
 
Nothing, nothing.

429
00:40:15,000 --> 00:40:17,000
Em hatine ku em li vir rûnin, mezinê malê kî ne?
 
We have come to sit here, who are the elders of the house?

430
00:40:17,000 --> 00:40:21,000
Werin, werin, xûn şirîn e.
 
Come, come, the blood is sweet (you are lovable).

431
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:23,000
Ser çava, ser çava.
 
You are welcome, upon my eyes.

432
00:40:23,000 --> 00:40:26,000
Werin pêş, telmoka me re çêke.
 
Come forward, film our telmok (woven bag/sack).

433
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:30,000
Telmoka me re çêke.
 
Film our telmok.

434
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:33,000
Werin, werin, werin, werin.
 
Come, come, come, come.

435
00:40:33,000 --> 00:40:35,000
Werin kela kê kê ma.
 
Come, whose... (stumbling) remains.

436
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:37,000
Emê herin ew çopê me re çêke.
 
We will go, film that stick/rubbish for us.

437
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:40,000
Ser serî, hatina we ser çava.
 
Upon my head, your arrival is upon my eyes (welcome).

438
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:42,000
Na, na, telmoka me re çêke bes e.
 
No, no, just film our telmok, that's enough.

439
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:44,000
Telma xweş e.
 
The telm (woven sack) is nice.

440
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:47,000
Erê hevalno, taban em gihiştin mala Xalo.
 
Yes friends, naturally we arrived at Uncle's (Xalo's) house.

441
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:49,000
Emê li cem Xalo rûniştine, niha emê qehwekî vexwin.
 
We are sitting with Uncle, now we will drink a coffee.

442
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:54,000
Li ber vê bayê hênik. Maşallah, ciyekî pir kîbar e.
 
In this cool breeze. Mashallah, it is a very decent place.

443
00:40:54,000 --> 00:40:59,000
Xalo, gundê we çiqas mal... malê têda, sekan?
 
Uncle, your village, how many houses... houses are in it,
residents?

444
00:40:59,000 --> 00:41:03,000
Welle haliyen (niha), yanî... em çar pênc mal in.
 
Well currently, meaning... we are four or five households.

445
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:05,000
Bes ê pirr jê derketin e.
 
But most of them have left.

446
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:06,000
Derketin e, ne?
 
They left, right?

447
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:07,000
Ji neçariyê derketin e.
 
They left out of necessity.

448
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:10,000
Gundê we bi çi tê naskirin? Bi çi me'rûf e?
 
What is your village known for? What is it famous for?

449
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:13,000
Welle me'rûfa xwe xweş e, bi darê zeytûna ye.
 
Well, its fame is nice, it is for olive trees.

450
00:41:13,000 --> 00:41:14,000
Zeytûn li çiyayê şîn dibin?
 
Do olives grow on the mountain?

451
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:17,000
Belê, zeytûnê reş yê şîn derdikevin.
 
Yes, black olives and green ones come out.

452
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:18,000
Eslê xwe hawa ye.
 
Its origin is like that.

453
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:23,000
Gundê we pir bilind e, û... çep e, çep, rêka xwe çep e.
 
Your village is very high, and... it's steep/off-hand,
steep, its road is steep.

454
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:27,000
Welle, rê yekîşte, yanî teqriben pênc kîlometre dahrê
kepse... dahrê kepse û dahrê kevir e.
 
Well, the road is barely... meaning approximately five
kilometers of unpaved road... unpaved road and rocky road.

455
00:41:27,000 --> 00:41:28,000
Sînor ji vir çiqas dûr e?
 
How far is the border from here?

456
00:41:28,000 --> 00:41:29,000
Pênc kîlometre?
 
Five kilometers?

457
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:31,000
Pênc kîlometre.
 
Five kilometers.

458
00:41:31,000 --> 00:41:33,000
Ko rêka me ne dûr bûya, emê biçûna wê derê jî.
 
If our road wasn't far, we would have gone there too.

459
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:35,000
Emê biçin wê derê jî.
 
We will go there too.

460
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:36,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

461
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:42,000
Te çi silavê te ji bo milet ra heye, te divê çi... ey em
şandin cem te, te divê çi bêjî?
 
What greetings do you have for the people, what do you want
to... since we were sent to you, what do you want to say?

462
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:44,000
Ez dixwazim silavên min ji wan re hene.
 
I want (to say) I have greetings for them.

463
00:41:44,000 --> 00:41:45,000
Giştî ko re?
 
Generally to whom?

464
00:41:45,000 --> 00:41:48,000
Xadê miletê me xweşî tê de hebe.
 
May God grant goodness among our people.

465
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:49,000
Bi kêfxweş bin.
 
May they be happy.

466
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:50,000
Emîn.
 
Amen.

467
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:51,000
Wextê xweş bigire.
 
Have a good time.

468
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:53,000
Emîn, saeta te xweş.
 
Amen, may your time be happy.

469
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:56,000
Xaltîk, tu gotina te hene? Tu kê bikî, tu silav kî bişînî?
 
Aunty, do you have any words? Who do you want to... who do
you want to send greetings to?

470
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:59,000
Ez jî dişînim, ehlen we sehlen, ji giya re, ji wa re jî, ji
wa re jî.
 
I also send them, welcome, to everyone, to them too, to them
too.

471
00:41:59,000 --> 00:42:03,000
Silavê min ji giya re hene, û ji zarokê min re jî hene li
Elmanya.
 
My greetings are for everyone, and for my children in
Germany too.

472
00:42:03,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Û ji ewên şandina ra jî hene.
 
And for those who sent (help) too.

473
00:42:06,000 --> 00:42:07,000
Ji milet giya re heye.
 
It is for the whole nation.

474
00:42:07,000 --> 00:42:08,000
Ê Kurmanc.
 
The Kurds.

475
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:11,000
Saet xweş. Silavên te gihîştinê. Xaltîk silavên we
gihîştinê.
 
Bless you. Your greetings reached them. Aunty, your
greetings reached them.

476
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:12,000
Inşallah.
 
God willing.

477
00:42:12,000 --> 00:42:13,000
Saeta te jî xweş.
 
May your time be happy too.

478
00:42:13,000 --> 00:42:20,000
Saeta we xweş.
 
May your time be happy.

479
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:23,000
Erê hevalno, taban ev hewş e jî, kevnar e, mala Xalo.
 
Yes friends, naturally this courtyard too, is ancient,
Uncle's house.

480
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:27,000
Dîkûra gund e, o seke, hevalno li bini.
 
It is the decor of the village, oh look, friends look below.

481
00:42:27,000 --> 00:42:32,000
Seke, resmê gundê kevnar e, ne?
 
Look, it is a picture of the ancient village, isn't it?

482
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:32,000
Çûk û serî genim e.
 
Film that.

483
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:35,000
Çûk û serî genim e.
 
Birds and wheat heads.

484
00:42:35,000 --> 00:42:39,000
Taban hevalno, li vir jî... lê bigire hevalî.
 
Naturally friends, here too... hold this, my friend.

485
00:42:39,000 --> 00:42:47,000
Hevalno ev nivîsî jî... seke, bixwîne, bi Erebî ye, beş
şûretê xwe, manê xwe bi Tirkî ne, weke gund e.
 
Friends, this writing too... look, read it, it is in Arabic
(script), but its form, its meaning is Turkish, like the
village.

486
00:42:47,000 --> 00:42:51,000
Hawa dibê bare, usta jî Tirk e darê da... hatin vî darê...
 
They say it like this, the master too is Turkish, regarding
the tree... came to this tree...

487
00:42:51,000 --> 00:42:56,000
Li vir yopê digirtin, çu wek em darên Lubnanê dişuxulin.
 
Here they used to take the... just like we work the trees of
Lebanon.

488
00:42:56,000 --> 00:43:00,000
Çû wek em Lubnanê diçûn dişuxilîn, meselan me yopê digirt,
me mişmiş diçinin.
 
Just like we used to go to Lebanon to work, for example we
handled the... we picked apricots.

489
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:04,000
Ê, ew jî hatine, li vî darê, vî yopiyê girtine.
 
Uh, they too came, to this tree, they took this job/crop.

490
00:43:04,000 --> 00:43:06,000
Ê yopê girtî Tirk bî.
 
The one who took the job was a Turk.

491
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:09,000
Kû hevalî me, me agirê puxarêk di vir da ji heye.
 
Where is our friend, we also have a fireplace fire in here.

492
00:43:09,000 --> 00:43:13,000
Viro, ji şevê, hevalno.
 
Here, for the night, friends.

493
00:43:13,000 --> 00:43:15,000
Taban, maşallah.
 
Naturally, mashallah.

494
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Şevê xwe jî emê li vir dikin puxar e, didiye?
 
We spend our nights here too, it is a fireplace, you see?

495
00:43:18,000 --> 00:43:23,000
Puxarê xwe bibîne, maşallah, xortikê işê xwe nîzamî ye. Mebû
işê xortikê nîzamî ye.
 
Look at his fireplace, mashallah, the young man's work is
orderly. Indeed the young man's work is orderly.

496
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:30,000
Û vî gundê jî, ew hevalno, yanî, kûk çend mal in, û bilind û
dûr.
 
And this village too, friends, meaning, just a few houses,
and high and far.

497
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:31,000
De wer...
 
Come on then...

498
00:43:31,000 --> 00:43:34,000
Boy bavê Kelewî min.
 
For my Kelewi's father.

499
00:43:34,000 --> 00:43:35,000
Zeyno.
 
Zeyno.

500
00:43:35,000 --> 00:43:38,000
Aldar, sêr, sêr, kaka ye, kaka ye.
 
Aldar, look, look, it's a brother, it's a brother.

501
00:43:38,000 --> 00:43:40,000
Boy bike, boy bike, kaka.
 
Do 'boy' (wave/gesture), do 'boy', brother.

502
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:41,000
Navê wî çiye?
 
What is his name?

503
00:43:41,000 --> 00:43:42,000
Aldar.
 
Aldar.

504
00:43:42,000 --> 00:43:43,000
Aldar?
 
Aldar?

505
00:43:43,000 --> 00:43:45,000
Hisên, Hisên, kaka ye.
 
Hussein, Hussein, it's a brother.

506
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:48,000
Xwedê emrê wî dirêj pê de. Xwedê emrê wî dirêj pê de.
 
May God give him a long life. May God give him a long life.

507
00:43:48,000 --> 00:43:53,000
Saet xweş.
 
Bless you.

508
00:43:53,000 --> 00:44:02,000
Arê hevalno, taban vê malbatê jî, malbatek feqîr e, nexweşî
jî di nav gund de hene. Xwedê pêxember...
 
Yes friends, naturally this family too, is a poor family,
there is also illness within the village. God, the
Prophet...

509
00:44:02,000 --> 00:44:05,000
Jê razî be, Xwedê emrê kî dirêj pê de.
 
Be pleased with him, may God give him a long life.

510
00:44:05,000 --> 00:44:10,000
Û inşallah, de ta kesî me ra, ew kir, û dîsa emê xobwa gine
xortik. Xêrxwaz pirr in di gund de da.
 
And God willing, gave to someone for us, he did that, and
again we will... the young man. There are many
philanthropists in the village.

511
00:44:10,000 --> 00:44:16,000
Berî vê jî me... gundê şar o, me xelkê rojava harîkar kir,
xêrxwaz hebin, tebera kirin.
 
Before this too we... the village/city, we helped the people
of the West (Rojava), may the philanthropists exist, they
donated.

512
00:44:16,000 --> 00:44:19,000
Û inşallah dîsa tiştek ew bî, û dîsa emê werin cem te. Emê
xwa cem te ginin.
 
And God willing if something happens again, and again we
will come to you. We will come to you.

513
00:44:19,000 --> 00:44:20,000
Temam?
 
Okay?

514
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:21,000
Saeta we xweş.
 
May your time be happy (Thank you).

515
00:44:21,000 --> 00:44:25,000
Xwedê se'dê wekî dîtî, her kesî be, û Xwedê emrê kî dirêj
bide.
 
May God [grant] happiness as seen, to everyone, and may God
give a long life.

516
00:44:25,000 --> 00:44:27,000
Xwedê te'bana we...
 
God [reward] your fatigue...

517
00:44:27,000 --> 00:44:29,000
De te'ban na, welle xortik.
 
It is not fatigue, really young man.

518
00:44:29,000 --> 00:44:36,000
Da me kanî, em kelak wa bizgirin, milet me re ew kir, û dîsa
bi çavê xwe emê werin.
 
So we can, hold your side/support you, the people did that
for us, and again with our own eyes (willingly) we will
come.

519
00:44:36,000 --> 00:44:38,000
Saeta her yekî xweş, li me sêr dike.
 
May the time of everyone who watches us be happy.

520
00:44:38,000 --> 00:44:42,000
Wallahî berî vê me re teqsîr nekirne, wele em çûn şar o jî,
me gundana jî ew kir.
 
I swear before this they did not neglect us, really we went
to the city too, and the villages, we did that.

521
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:43,000
Saeta giya xweş.
 
Bless everyone.

522
00:44:43,000 --> 00:44:46,000
Xwedê emrê kî dirêj pê de.
 
May God give him a long life.

523
00:44:46,000 --> 00:44:51,000
Arê hevalno, taban emê vîdyo xwe xîtam kin, li cem mala
Xalo.
 
Yes friends, naturally we will conclude our video, at
Uncle's house.

524
00:44:51,000 --> 00:44:56,000
Emê noha dilax taden jî, nav gund emê du we re têkin, teswîr
kin.
 
We will now... the name of the village, we will
record/picture it for you twice.

525
00:44:56,000 --> 00:45:01,000
Xalo gotina te dan hene, te kê bike?
 
Uncle do you have any sayings, what do you want to do?

526
00:45:01,000 --> 00:45:04,000
Welle, daxwaz dikim miletê me kurmanc gî bi tifaq bin, mala
xwe...
 
Well, I wish that our Kurdish nation are all united, their
home...

527
00:45:04,000 --> 00:45:05,000
İnşallah.
 
God willing.

528
00:45:05,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Û hevalno jî noha me derkevin.
 
And friends too, now we are leaving.

529
00:45:06,000 --> 00:45:07,000
İnşallah.
 
God willing.

530
00:45:07,000 --> 00:45:09,000
Aferîna me xweş bû, bi we re jî bî.
 
Our praise/time was good, and with you too.

531
00:45:09,000 --> 00:45:13,000
Xweş bibe, xweş bibe, inşallah giya vegerin, noha me hîştî
xelkê miletê pir vegeriya ware ziware.
 
Be happy, be happy, God willing everyone returns, now we
left many people, the nation returned to the sacred places.

532
00:45:13,000 --> 00:45:15,000
İnşallah, inşallah.
 
God willing, God willing.

533
00:45:15,000 --> 00:45:16,000
Yê rind bî hêşta.
 
It will be even better.

534
00:45:16,000 --> 00:45:19,000
Arê. Arê hevalno, taban vê gund o jî...
 
Yes. Yes friends, naturally this village too...

535
00:45:19,000 --> 00:45:21,000
Xalo, eh nako me re hawal de.
 
Uncle, uh tell us now.

536
00:45:21,000 --> 00:45:24,000
Xalo te gû bajarok heye, li Rûsya navê xwe çiye?
 
Uncle you said there is a town, in Russia, what is its name?

537
00:45:24,000 --> 00:45:25,000
Tatar e.
 
It is Tatar.

538
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:29,000
Tatar. Dibe eşîrek li Rûsya heye, navê xwe Tatar e.
 
Tatar. He says there is a tribe in Russia, its name is
Tatar.

539
00:45:29,000 --> 00:45:31,000
Wakî melek e, wakî dar a.
 
Like a king/angel, like a tree.

540
00:45:31,000 --> 00:45:35,000
Vê gund o, wê manê pê nav kirin.
 
This village, was named with that meaning.

541
00:45:35,000 --> 00:45:36,000
Arê wilo.
 
Yes, like that.

542
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:39,000
Gûr Xalo zane, gûr melûmatê xwe ser, wanî nawaye.
 
According to Uncle's knowledge, according to his
information, it is not like that [sic].

543
00:45:39,000 --> 00:45:42,000
Gûrkî da wa dibê gotin.
 
As they say.

544
00:45:42,000 --> 00:45:44,000
Wê manê nople kirin Tatar.
 
That meaning [was used to] name it Tatar.

545
00:45:44,000 --> 00:45:49,000
Xwe bi me re bin, inşallah vîdyo vîdyo me xweş, hecer. Le
heynê mişwarê me jî dûr e.
 
Be with us, God willing our video is good, stone/solid. But
look, our journey is far.

546
00:45:49,000 --> 00:45:51,000
Çavê we maç dikim. Bay bay kî Xalo.
 
I kiss your eyes. Do a 'bye bye' Uncle.

547
00:45:51,000 --> 00:45:52,000
Oxir be.
 
Bon voyage (Goodbye).

548
00:45:52,000 --> 00:46:03,000
Saeta we xweş.
 
Bless you.

549
00:46:03,000 --> 00:46:05,000
Saeta we xweş, Xwedê ji we razî be.
 
Bless you, may God be pleased with you.

550
00:46:05,000 --> 00:46:10,000
Saet xweş.
 
Bless you.

